Think of Pages as something you create as needed inside the SharePoint Site.
For example, your Budget Approval Site might start with:
Home page

Then you create additional pages:
    Budget Process
    Approval Guidelines
    FAQ
    Help
    Contact Us

So you might end up with 6 pages.

1)How do you create another page?
Typically:

    SharePoint Site → New → Page
    Then:
            Choose a page/template
            Give it a name
            Add sections
            Add Web Parts
            Publish the page
    The pages are stored in the site's Site Pages library.

Normal SharePoint Page = UI configuration, no code.
Custom functionality/UI = SPFx development/code.
